  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nYou do not need to submit invoices together with your income tax return. Under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), specifically Section 23, the filing of the income tax return does not require the attachment of invoices or other supporting documents unless specifically requested by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) during an audit or examination.\n\nHowever, it is essential to maintain proper records, including invoices, as they may be required for verification purposes if the BIR conducts an audit. Keeping these documents organized and readily available will help ensure compliance and facilitate any necessary reviews by tax authorities.\n\n### Relevant Facts / Assumptions\nThe factual circumstances have not been fully described. The analysis is based on the question as presented.\n\n### Alternative Interpretations\nNo alternative interpretations identified from the available indexed authorities.\n\n### Position Strength\nPosition strength is preliminary and subject to full fact pattern verification.",
